    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d238">

                <pb facs="0331" n="317" sameAs="frus:frus1948v06/pg317"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BC Indonesia/9–248: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consulate General at
                        Batavia</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-09-03T17:00:00-04:00">September 3,
                            1948—5 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>399. Usgoc 134, Gocus 364<anchor n="1" xml:id="d238-f1"/> and 365.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d238-f2"/> In light your comment Neth draft agreement would not
                    prove acceptable even as basis for opening discussion, Dept agrees you should
                    not urge Neth Del present this text GOC.</p>
                <p>Reference garble in Gocus 360.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d238-f3"/> Dept’s only desire
                    (para 3, Gocus 365) is that at no stage should USDel paper be discussed with one
                    party without discussing with other.</p>
                <pb facs="0332" n="318" xml:id="pg318"/>
                <p>Re last sentence para 3, Gocus 365, Dept does not believe US plan should be
                    presented as Neth Del plan.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
